        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telemetry): record session.ended trajectory event after flush, not inline with model.completed",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #102014 — the `session.ended` trajectory event timestamp equals the last\n`model.completed` timestamp, making session cleanup duration invisible in traces.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`session.ended` was recorded inside the try block immediately after\n`model.completed` in the same synchronous execution. Both events shared the\nsame millisecond timestamp because `new Date().toISOString()` was called\nsynchronously.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Defer `session.ended` from the try block to after cleanup in the finally block\n2. Emit `session.cleanup_completed` before `session.ended` so cleanup completion\n   is visible in trajectory exports\n3. Carry `attemptTrajectoryTerminal.status` and `terminalError` into the\n   deferred event\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\nTrajectory export from live agent session on this branch:\n\n```\nseq=5  model.completed                 06.695\nseq=6  trace.artifacts                 06.698\nseq=7  session.cleanup_completed       06.860   ← cleanup done (162ms later)\nseq=8  session.ended                   06.860   ← session terminated\n```\n\n`session.cleanup_completed` proves cleanup ran between `model.completed`\nand `session.ended`. The 162ms gap reflects actual teardown and state\npersistence, not just synchronous overhead.\n\n### Autoreview (claude-sonnet-5)\n\n```\nautoreview --mode branch --engine claude --model claude-sonnet-5\n→ patch is correct (0.95), no accepted/actionable findings\n```\n\n- [x] `oxfmt --check` passes\n- [x] `oxlint` passes\n- [x] `git diff --check` passes\n- [x] autoreview clean (claude-sonnet-5, 0.95)",
